{"at":1793546079681,"pos":2,"ticket":1,"by":{"kind":"user","id":"owner"},"fact":{"type":"filed","title":"Add slugify: turn a title into a URL slug","body":"Blog posts need a URL slug made from their title.\n\nAdd `slugify(text)` in `src/slug.ts`. It takes a title and gives a slug:\n\n- lowercase, ASCII only\n- words joined by one `-`\n- no leading or trailing `-`\n- letters that are not ASCII fold to their plain form when they can, so `Çay Şeker` gives `cay-seker`\n\nAnything left that is not a letter or a digit separates words. A title with nothing usable gives an empty string."}}
